  "name": "Tipo de Documento de Identidad",
  "source": "Anexo 8 (catálogo 06) from the 'Catálogos' sheet of perunio-facturador/resources/reglas/reglas-validacion-cpe-2026-08-26.xlsx: thirteen códigos, 0 through H, all here. H (CPP) has been valid since 2023-01-01 (Control de Cambios of 29.11.2022). The GRE workbook's own Catálogos sheet (perunio-facturador/resources/reglas/reglas-validacion-gre-2026-09-25.xlsx) stops at G, and a guía's destinatario is checked against that listado (ERROR 2760), so treat H on a guía as unconfirmed. Descripciones are SUNAT's, with its en dashes normalised to hyphens — including código 6's 'Contributentes', SUNAT's own misspelling; `label` carries 'RUC' and is what a UI renders. E is the TAM, Tarjeta Andina de Migración, not NITE as an earlier Go copy had it. props.numberPattern is set only where a length rule is actually documented and enforced today (RUC and DNI); null means the número is not constrained here, not that SUNAT leaves it unvalidated. The `select` subset is exactly what the issuance UI offers today — widening it is a data-only change once each código gains a numberPattern.",
  "codePattern": "^[0-9A-H]$",
  "entries": [
    {
      "code": "0",
      "label": "Sin documento",
      "description": "DOC.TRIB.NO.DOM.SIN.RUC",
      "capabilities": [
